# 🛡️ AsohCloak

**AsohCloak** is a authentication & authorization REST API built with Spring Boot and Keycloak. It exists first and foremost as a hands-on deep dive into building a **production-style Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) system** on top of Keycloak — with School Management features layered on top once the security foundation is solid. 🎓

---

## 🎯 Project Goal

The primary purpose of this project is to **master authentication and authorization with Spring Boot + Keycloak** — understanding how to delegate identity, token issuance, and access control entirely to Keycloak rather than hand-rolling auth logic. School Management functionality (students, bursars, admins, academic records, etc.) is the *next* phase, built on top of this security foundation.

> 🔐 **Design principle:** Keycloak owns *everything* about security in this system — user credentials, token issuance, brute-force protection, and role management. AsohCloak's Spring Boot layer is a resource server + a thin orchestrator that talks to Keycloak's Admin API. No passwords or tokens are minted by this application itself.

---

## ✨ Key Features

- 📝 **Registration** — create a new user account (provisioned through Keycloak)
- 🔑 **Login** — issues short-lived access & refresh tokens *only* during the login step
- 🚪 **Logout** — revokes the active session/tokens
- 🔒 **Forgot Password** — initiate a password-reset flow
- ♻️ **Reset Password** — complete the password reset
- ⛔ **Block User** — administratively disable an account
- ✅ **Unblock User** — re-enable a previously blocked account
- 🔢 **Verify OTP Code** — one-time-passcode verification for passwordless / 2FA flows
- 🔁 **Resend OTP Code** — request a fresh OTP when the previous one expires
- ✉️ **Send Magic Link** — passwordless login link delivered by email
- 🪄 **Login via Magic Link** — authenticate by clicking the emailed link
- 🎭 **Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)** — fine-grained authorization driven by Keycloak realm roles

---

## 🧰 Tech Stack

| Category | Technology |
|---|---|
| ☕ Language | **Java 25** |
| 🍃 Framework | **Spring Boot 4.1.1** |
| 🔐 Identity & Access Management | **Keycloak** (Admin REST API + custom SPI for OTP / magic-link) |
| 🛡️ Security | **Spring Security** (OAuth2 Resource Server, JWT validation) |
| 🗄️ Database | **PostgreSQL** |
| 📦 ORM | **Spring Data JPA** / Hibernate |
| 🧬 Schema Migrations | **Flyway** |
| 🗺️ Object Mapping | **MapStruct** |
| ✂️ Boilerplate Reduction | **Lombok** |
| ⚡ Caching / Ephemeral Storage | **Redis** *(planned — not yet wired into the project; intended for OTP codes & magic-link tokens)* |
| 📧 Transactional Email | **Resend** |
| 🪣 Object Storage | **MinIO** |
| 📖 API Documentation | **springdoc-openapi** (Swagger UI) |
| 🐳 Containerization | **Docker** (multi-stage build) |
| 🏗️ Build Tool | **Maven** |

---

## 🏛️ Architecture Overview

```
┌─────────────┐        ┌──────────────────┐        ┌─────────────┐
│   React     │──────▶ │   AsohCloak API   │──────▶ │  Keycloak   │
│  Frontend   │  REST  │ (Resource Server) │ Admin  │  (Identity  │
└─────────────┘        └────────┬──────────┘  API   │   Provider) │
                                 │                    └─────────────┘
                          ┌──────┴──────┐
                          │             │
                     ┌────▼───┐   ┌─────▼─────┐
                     │Postgres│   │   MinIO    │
                     │ (data) │   │ (storage)  │
                     └────────┘   └────────────┘
```

- AsohCloak validates every incoming request as an **OAuth2 resource server**, checking JWTs issued by Keycloak.
- Registration, login, block/unblock, and password flows call **Keycloak's Admin REST API** rather than managing credentials locally.
- OTP verification and Magic Link login are implemented as a **custom Keycloak SPI** (a separate Maven project, `asohcloak-keycloak-providers`), keeping Keycloak as the single source of truth for auth even for flows it doesn't support out of the box.

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- ☕ JDK 25
- 🐳 Docker & Docker Compose
- 📦 Maven (or use the bundled `./mvnw` wrapper)
- 🗄️ A running PostgreSQL instance (or use `docker-compose`)
- 🔐 A running Keycloak instance with a configured realm

### 1. Clone the repo

```bash
git clone https://github.com/asohyannick/asohCloak.git
cd asohCloak
```

### 2. Configure your environment

Copy the example env file and fill in real values:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

Fill in your Postgres, Resend, MinIO, and Keycloak credentials in `.env`. **Never commit your real `.env` file.**

### 3. Run the app

```bash
./mvnw spring-boot:run
```

Or via Docker:

```bash
docker build -t asohcloak .
docker run --env-file .env -p 8080:8080 asohcloak
```

### 4. Explore the API

Once running, Swagger UI is available at:

```
http://localhost:8080/api/v1/swagger-ui.html
```

